[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/literalynn/Hellraiser-Revivals-Ketamine-Menu/main/docs/hero.jpg[/img]

[size=6][b][color=#AC6EE2]Hellraiser Revival's Ketamine Menu[/color][/b][/size]
[size=3]A clean in-game trainer for Clive Barker's Hellraiser: Revival.
One file, press [b][color=#F89FCD]Insert[/color][/b], done.[/size][/center]

[line]

[size=4][b][color=#F89FCD]Important[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Single-player only.[/b] The menu has no online features, but the game talks to its publisher's online services:
play in [b]Steam offline mode[/b] while it is installed.
[*][b]Back up your saves[/b] before you start: [code]%LOCALAPPDATA%\Hellraiser\Saved\SaveGames[/code]
[*]No game file is ever modified. Uninstalling = deleting the files listed below.
[/list]

[line]

[size=4][b][color=#AC6EE2]Features[/color][/b][/size]
Every option finds the game's data [b]by name[/b] at runtime. If a game update removes something, that option is greyed out with
the reason in a tooltip instead of crashing.

[b]Player[/b]
[list]
[*]God mode, infinite health, health slider
[*]No sprint cooldown (the game has no stamina)
[*]Invisible to enemies
[*]One-hit kill, damage multiplier
[/list]
[b]Combat[/b]
[list]
[*]Infinite ammo, unbreakable melee weapons
[*]Genesis Configuration powers with no Suffering cost, no power cooldown, refill Suffering
[/list]
[b]Movement[/b]
[list]
[*]Fly and noclip towards where you look, with your usual movement keys or gamepad
[*]Free camera (your character stays in place)
[*]Speed and jump height multipliers
[*]3 saved positions + teleport to any level checkpoint
[/list]
[b]ESP[/b]
[list]
[*]Enemies: box, health bar, name, distance, skeleton, head marker, chams, snaplines, off-screen arrows
[*]World: items on the ground, loot containers, save points
[/list]
[b]Inventory[/b]
[list]
[*]Add or remove money
[*]Give any item: ammo, weapons, upgrades, healing, materials (list built from the game itself)
[*]Unlock weapon skins & charms
[/list]
[b]World / Progress[/b]
[list]
[*]Time scale, freeze enemies, kill enemies nearby, field of view, hide HUD
[*]See active and completed objectives, complete one, change the shop level
[/list]
[b]Quality of life[/b]
[list]
[*]Any switch can get its own hotkey (works with the menu closed, with a small notification)
[*]Rebindable menu key, UI scale, settings saved automatically
[*]Footer with game version, CPU, GPU, RAM, resolution and FPS
[/list]

[line]

[size=4][b][color=#F89FCD]Installation[/color][/b][/size]
[b]Vortex:[/b] click [i]Mod Manager Download[/i], then enable and deploy the mod. That's it.

[b]Manual:[/b]
[list=1]
[*]In Steam: right-click the game → [i]Manage[/i] → [i]Browse local files[/i].
[*]Extract the zip [b]into that folder[/b] (the one that contains the [code]Hellraiser[/code] folder). [code]winmm.dll[/code] must end up in:
[code]Clive Barker's Hellraiser - Revival\Hellraiser\Binaries\Win64\winmm.dll[/code]
(next to [code]Hellraiser-Win64-Shipping.exe[/code]).
[*]Start the game, load a save, press [b]Insert[/b].
[/list]
No Visual C++ redistributable or launcher needed.

[line]

[size=4][b][color=#AC6EE2]Usage[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Insert[/b] opens / closes the menu (rebindable in Settings). While it is open, the mouse controls the menu and the game ignores your input.
[*]Hover any option to see what it does, or why it is unavailable.
[*]Settings are saved to [code]KetamineMenu.ini[/code] next to the DLL. [i]Settings → Reset configuration[/i] restores the defaults.
[*]Giving key items or completing objectives can break scripted sequences: [b]save first[/b].
[/list]

[line]

[size=4][b][color=#F89FCD]Compatibility[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Game:[/b] tested with 1.1.1.227384 (October 2026 update) and 1.0.1.227219, Steam.
[*][b]Renderer:[/b] DirectX 12 (default) and DirectX 11.
[*][b]Other mods:[/b] uses [code]winmm.dll[/code], so it doesn't collide with ReShade ([code]dxgi.dll[/code]) or UE4SS ([code]dwmapi.dll[/code]).
[*][b]Frame generation[/b] (DLSS-G, FSR, XeSS FG): supported; if the menu flickers, turn frame generation off.
[/list]

[line]

[size=4][b][color=#AC6EE2]Uninstall[/color][/b][/size]
[b]Vortex:[/b] remove the mod, then delete [code]KetamineMenu.ini[/code] and [code]KetamineMenu.log[/code] that the menu created.
[b]Manual:[/b] delete [code]winmm.dll[/code], [code]KetamineMenu-LICENSE.txt[/code], [code]KetamineMenu.ini[/code] and [code]KetamineMenu.log[/code]
from [code]Hellraiser\Binaries\Win64[/code].

[line]

[size=4][b][color=#F89FCD]Troubleshooting[/color][/b][/size]
[spoiler]
[b]Insert does nothing[/b]
Check that [code]winmm.dll[/code] is in [code]Hellraiser\Binaries\Win64[/code], not in the top game folder. Open [code]KetamineMenu.log[/code]
in the same folder: if it doesn't exist, the DLL wasn't loaded (check the folder and your antivirus).

[b]Everything is greyed out[/b]
Load a save first: most options need the player to exist. If the header says [i]Engine not hooked[/i], the game version changed in a
way the menu can't handle yet: post in the Bugs tab with your [code]KetamineMenu.log[/code].

[b]My antivirus flags the DLL[/b]
Trainers hook into a game's rendering and memory, which antivirus heuristics dislike. It's a false positive: the full source code is
on GitHub and every release is built from it by GitHub Actions. You can also build it yourself.
[/spoiler]

[b]Bug reports:[/b] use the Bugs tab here or [url=https://github.com/literalynn/Hellraiser-Revivals-Ketamine-Menu/issues]GitHub issues[/url],
with what you did, what happened, and your [code]KetamineMenu.log[/code] (overwritten each time the game starts).

